{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "18a358ab-d3b8-8894-8d71-f1f38fd85fd2",
  "created_at": "2026-02-25T17:24:58-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Janice Hazard",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Kevin Sousa",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T17:22:49-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, this is Kevin. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T17:22:53-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hello, Kevin, good evening. Um, my name is Janice Hazard. I am calling about the water on my street, Dean Avenue. It is still there, you know, from the storm."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T17:23:03-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, Dean Avenue. Which storm, the one last weekend?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T17:23:07-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, last weekend, the nor'easter, Saturday into Sunday. Now it is Wednesday and the water is still sitting. It is not going away."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T17:23:15-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Alright. Whereabouts on Dean are you seeing it?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T17:23:19-05:00",
      "duration": 20,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I live at 443 Dean Avenue, in the Fifth Ward. The street, it goes down, and all the water collects at the low end. Like a big pond. And the cars, they go so slow through it, a crawl, one by one. Sorry, one second, I still have my headset on, from my work call. [pause] I forget it every time."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T17:23:39-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No worries, I can hear you fine. So pooling at the low end, traffic crawling through. Is it getting into your property at all?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T17:23:48-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The apron, the driveway apron, it holds a puddle, and the puddle goes toward the garage door. Not inside yet, but it comes close. And this is not the first time, Kevin. Every storm it is the same, and nobody comes to fix it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T17:24:03-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, I hear you. I'm writing this down: 443 Dean Avenue, standing water at the low end of the street, backing up toward the driveway, slow traffic. I'll send it over to the crew supervisors as a drainage report."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T17:24:16-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you. Please, I would like somebody to really look at the drain. Do the crews work on weekends? Because if it rains again, I think it will be worse."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T17:24:26-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "They do get out on weekends when things are bad, especially after a storm, but they're stretched thin right now with everything that came down. I can't tell you the exact day they'll get to Dean, but it'll be flagged."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T17:24:40-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. I understand. It is just, we keep waiting. My number is 401-555-0158, if they need me."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T17:24:46-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it, 401-555-0158, Janice. I've got it on the report."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T17:24:50-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you, Kevin. You have a good evening. [pause] Oh, my headset, still on. Goodbye."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T17:24:56-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You too. Bye now."
    }
  ],
